   415   *
   416   * FILTER_SET: Store @p number into an empty slot in @p filter. Returns
   417   * @c 1 on success, or @c 0 if no spare slot was available.
   418   *
   419   * FILTER_CLEAR: Remove @p number from filter if it exists.
   420   *
   421   * FILTER_GET: Search for @p number in @p filter. Returns @c 1 if found,
   422   * or @c 0 if not found.
   423   *
   424   * @param filter The filter object.
   425   * @param number The option number to set, get or clear in @p filter.
   426   * @param op     The operation to apply to @p filter and @p number.
